End-to-end reachability corroborates this: hosts in the Campus 1 VLANs (e.g., 172.16.20.10, 172.16.10.7) successfully ping off-campus subnets (e.g., 10.6.0.3) with 0% loss, indicating forwarding is functioning across the core. If router16 were down or had lost OSPF, these routes would be absent and reachability would fail.

